## Living docs (read in order at session start)
1. `checkpoint.md` — where the last session left off
2. `tasks.md` — in progress, next, backlog, done
3. `lessons.md` — append-only learnings (consult when stuck)

At session end: **overwrite** `checkpoint.md`, update `tasks.md` (move finished items to Done
with date + SHA), and **append** surprises to `lessons.md` (newest on top). If context runs
short mid-task, write the checkpoint first, then continue.

## Workflow
- Gate: `{{gate.lint}} && {{gate.test}}`. CI runs the same targets — run them before
  reporting work finished.
- Dev standards come from the `{{marketplace.name}}` plugins, enabled for this repo in
  `.claude/settings.json`. Follow them:

| Skill | Use it when |
|---|---|
| `{{skills.committing-work}}` | Naming a branch, writing or signing a commit, fixups |
| `{{skills.pull-requests}}` | Opening, filling, or merging a PR |
| `{{skills.reviewing-prs}}` | Reviewing someone else's PR |
| `{{skills.code-testing}}` | Adding or changing tests; regression test before a bug fix |
| `{{skills.ponytail-fix}}` | The gate or CI is red |
| `{{skills.setup-ci}}` | Changing CI or branch protection |
| `{{skills.writing-readmes}}` | Editing a README |
| `{{skills.changelog}}` | Recording user-visible changes in `CHANGELOG.md` |
| `{{skills.gitignore}}` | Adding ignore rules |

## Python
- Out-of-source venv at `~/.virtualenvs/{{repo dir name}}`, set by the committed `.envrc`
  (one venv per checkout, so worktrees never share one). Run `direnv allow` once.
- `uv add <pkg>` for deps; `uv run <cmd>` to run. Never `pip install` outside the venv.
- Secrets and per-developer overrides go in `.envrc.local` (gitignored). Never commit
  credentials, workspace hosts, or tokens.
